{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q3028867","formula":"P₂","hill":"P2","elements":["P"],"composition":{"P":2.0},"names":{"en":"Diphosphorus","ru":"Дифосфор"},"descriptions":{"en":"Diphosphorus is an inorganic chemical with the chemical formula P2. Unlike nitrogen, its lighter pnictogen neighbor which forms a stable N2 molecule with a nitrogen to nitrogen triple bond, phosphorus prefers a tetrahedral form P4 because P-P pi-bonds are high in energy. Diphosphorus is, therefore, very reactive with a bond-dissociation energy (117 kcal/mol or 490 kJ/mol) half that of dinitrogen.","ru":"Дифосфор — химическое соединение, состоящее из двух атомов фосфора соединённых тройной связью с химической формулой P2. Является фосфорным аналогом двухатомного азота N2. Очень реактивен, его энергия диссоциации связи (117 ккал/моль или 490 кДж/моль) вдвое меньше, чем у двухатомного азота."},"fame":16,"pubchemCid":5460700,"mass":61.947524,"charge":0,"smiles":"P#P","inchikey":"FOBPTJZYDGNHLR-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"phosphanylidynephosphane","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"5460700","atoms":2,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.139,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"P"},{"x":1.139,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"P"}],"bonds":[[0,1,3]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3028867","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diphosphorus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%94%D0%B8%D1%84%D0%BE%D1%81%D1%84%D0%BE%D1%80","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"properties","name":"PubChem","url":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/5460700","license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},{"role":"structure","name":"PubChem 3D","url":"